I looked into the cmr files and noticed that for example cmr17 actually
is a font designed for 17.28pt. This opens the question of how to =
organize
fontshape defs again.

I currently think that it might be better to say something like

   <17.28>cmr17

instead of the white lie calling this <17>cmr17. Of course, this change =
would
mean that we need a bit more characters from the string pool, but on the =
other
hand it would allow to say something like

   <10->cmtt10%

and still the 17.28 size and all the others will be scaled correctly. =
For
Postscript fonts this will be even more important.

Any comments?

Frank

P.S. Has anybody seen the alpha test version at all?



